---
title: Incredible Roasted Shoulder of Lamb with Smashed Vegetables and Greens
servings: 6
prepTime: 25 min
cookTime: 4 hr 30 min
difficulty: Easy
Rating: 10/10
source: https://www.foodnetwork.com/recipes/jamie-oliver/incredible-roasted-shoulder-of-lamb-with-smashed-vegetables-and-greens-recipe-1953122
tags: Lamb
---

= Lamb =
Preheat your oven to 500°F.

Slash the fat side of the @lamb shoulder{2.5%lb} all over with a sharp knife.
Lay half the sprigs of @fresh rosemary{4%sprigs} and half the @garlic{1%bulb}(peeled and smashed)
on the bottom of a high-sided #roasting pan{}.
Rub the lamb all over @olive oil{} and season with @salt and @pepper.

Place it in the pan on top of the rosemary and garlic, and put the rest of the
rosemary and garlic on top of the lamb.
Tightly cover the tray with #aluminum foil{} and place in the oven.
Turn the oven down immediately to 325°F and cook for ~{4%hours} - it's done if you can pull the meat apart easily with 2 forks.

= Vegetables =
When the lamb is nearly cooked, peel @potatoes{1 1/2%pounds} and cut in large chunks.
Peel @carrots{3} and @rutabaga{1/2}, and cut all in small chunks.
Put the vegetables into a large pot of boiling salted water and boil hard
for ~{20%minutes} or so until you can slide a knife into the rutabaga easily.

Drain and allow to steam dry, retaining 1 cup of the cooking water.
Smash the vegetables up in the pan with most of the @butter{6%tbsp}.
If you prefer a smooth texture, add some of the reserved cooking water.
Spoon into a bowl, cover with foil and keep warm over a pan of simmering (clean) water.

= Sauce =
Remove the lamb from the oven and place it on a chopping board.
Cover it with foil, then a kitchen towel, and leave it to rest.

Put a large pan of salted water on to boil for the greens.

Pour away most of the fat from the roasting pan, discarding any bits of rosemary.
Put the roasting pan on the stovetop over medium heat and mix in the @all-purpose flour{1%tbsp}.
Add the @chicken stock{2%cups}, stirring and scraping all the sticky goodness off the bottom of the pan.
You won't need gallons of gravy, just a couple of flavorsome spoonfuls for each serving.
Add the @capers{2%tbsp}(soaked, drained and chopped), turn the heat down and simmer for a few minutes.

Finely chop the @fresh mint{1%bunch}(stems removed) and add it to the sauce with the
@red wine vinegar{2%tbsp} at the last minute then pour into a gravy boat.

Add the @fresh greens{1%pound}(white cabbage, savoy cabbage, or Brussels sprouts tops) to the pan
of fast-boiling salted water and cook for ~{4-5%minutes} to just soften them.
Drain and toss with @butter{1%tbsp} and a pinch of @salt and @pepper.

Place everything in the middle of the table, and shred the lamb in front of your guests. Absolutely delish!

